# How the snapshots were first taken: Generated support, not GNU Git blobs. Every file outside the unidata-romacs group is byte-for-byte the pinned GNU build's own installed output (share/emacs/32.0.50/lisp at gnu_commit, gunzipped where installed compressed; tools/build-gnu-oracle.sh builds it); the unidata-romacs group is that output passed through tools/lib/romacs_unidata.py. SHA-256 values attest these bytes. GNU generator/rule and input references below were traced at gnu_commit; eucjp-ms's generator reads an external glibc charmap. subdirs.el is build-aux/update-subdirs output for the pinned lisp/ directories in the C locale (the bytes crates/romacs-vm-gui/src/loadup.rs update_subdirs_writes_what_gnus_script_writes records). Earlier retained snapshots predated the pinned sources: tramp-loaddefs.el autoloaded a predicate tramp-cmds.el no longer defines, loaddefs.el, cus-load.el and finder-inf.el lacked newer GNU files and also listed Romacs's own files (whose autoloads lisp/session/romacs-bundled-autoloads.el now defines as it loads), and the tit quail tables came from another GNU's conversion, which the pinned binary does not reproduce.

